+# ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE
+
+## CVE-2026-92262 — False positive on MariaDB 10.11.19 (Debian bookworm)
+
+### Overview
+
+CVE-2026-92262 (MDEV-40362) is an issue where names carrying the legacy
+`#mysql50#` prefix were mixed up with ordinary database/table names in the
+table cache and on disk.
+
+### Why bookworm 1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1 does not need this patch
+
+The 10.11.19 orig tarball already contains upstream commit `f277eefa`
+(and its test follow-up `574ba66b`):
+
+- `check_table_name()` in `sql/table.cc` rejects the `#mysql50#` prefix on
+  names that are validly encoded.
+- `build_table_filename()` in `sql/sql_table.cc` returns an empty buffer for
+  invalid names and its callers handle that.
+- `sql/sql_db.cc` rejects creating databases with the `#mysql50#` prefix
+  (`error_if_mysql50_prefix`), and the `if (*db_name)` / `!*path` guards
+  are present.
+
+Re-applying a backport against the 10.11.19 source fails with
+"Reversed (or previously applied) patch detected" on most files.
+
+The Debian tracker still marks bookworm-security as vulnerable. That status
+has not caught up with the 10.11.19 source.
+
+### Verdict
+
+**No code patch required.** Treat scanner findings of CVE-2026-92262 on
+`mariadb` `1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1` as a **false positive**.
+
+This file is documentation only. It does not change MariaDB behavior.
+
+### References
+
+- https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92262
+- https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/f277eefa424850a8cba5c2371406047f6395e8bb
+- https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/574ba66b2d6c5d71db83d416677876e9b592858e
