+# ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE
+
+## CVE-2026-85746 — False positive on MariaDB 10.11.19 (Debian bookworm)
+
+### Overview
+
+CVE-2026-85746 is a buffer overflow in `AsText()` on deeply nested geometry
+collections (MDEV-40329). `Geometry::as_wkt()` and
+`Gis_geometry_collection::get_data_as_wkt()` used the unchecked
+`qs_append()` on space that had not been reserved.
+
+### Why bookworm 1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1 does not need this patch
+
+The 10.11.19 orig tarball already contains upstream commit `5c04ca55`:
+`sql/spatial.cc` uses the checked `wkt->append(')')`, `txt->append('(')`
+and `txt->append(')')`, and the MDEV-40329 regression test is already in
+`mysql-test/main/gis.test` and `mysql-test/main/gis.result`.
+Re-applying the upstream backport fails because the pre-fix context is gone
+(the patch reverse-applies cleanly).
+
+The Debian tracker still marks bookworm-security as vulnerable. That status
+has not caught up with the 10.11.19 source.
+
+### Verdict
+
+**No code patch required.** Treat scanner findings of CVE-2026-85746 on
+`mariadb` `1:10.11.19-0+deb12u1` as a **false positive**.
